\label{def:closure-operator}
Let $(L,\le)$ be a poset. A map $c:L\to L$ is a \emph{closure operator} if for all $x,y\in L$:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item (Extensive) $x \le c(x)$.
  \item (Monotone) $x \le y \Rightarrow c(x)\le c(y)$.
  \item (Idempotent) $c(c(x)) = c(x)$.
\end{enumerate}

